From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:21:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: support V4L2_DEC_CMD_START

The stateful decoder interface requires V4L2_DEC_CMD_START to resume
decoding after a drain, but the driver only implements
V4L2_DEC_CMD_STOP and returns -EINVAL for START. Clients such as
FFmpeg issue START after a seek, so the capture queue stays in the
"last buffer dequeued" state and decoding does not resume.

Implement START the same way as restarting the capture queue: put the
instance back into the running state, clear the last buffer state of
the capture queue and schedule the context if it is ready.
---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c    | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
index afd28be..40c9ebe 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_dec.c
@@ -888,6 +888,25 @@ static int vidioc_decoder_cmd(struct file *file, void *priv,
 			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->irqlock, flags);
 		}
 		break;
+	case V4L2_DEC_CMD_START:
+		if (cmd->flags != 0)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		if (!vb2_is_streaming(&ctx->vq_dst))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->irqlock, flags);
+		if (ctx->state == MFCINST_FINISHING ||
+		    ctx->state == MFCINST_FINISHED)
+			ctx->state = MFCINST_RUNNING;
+		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&dev->irqlock, flags);
+
+		vb2_clear_last_buffer_dequeued(&ctx->vq_dst);
+
+		if (s5p_mfc_ctx_ready(ctx))
+			set_work_bit_irqsave(ctx);
+		s5p_mfc_hw_call(dev->mfc_ops, try_run, dev);
+		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-- 
